# Build output. Both names: the README publishes to out/, and -o takes whatever you type, so a
# 49 MB exe is otherwise one `git add -A` away from the history.
bin/
obj/
publish/
out/
*.user

# Velopack output. Same hazard, larger: a full .nupkg, a portable .zip and a Setup.exe per version,
# ~90 MB each, so a couple of test versions is already a third of a gigabyte.
releases/

# Capture scratch for READMEs and posts. Mostly gameplay video, which is the worst thing to put in
# git: 21 MB of it here already, it never diffs, and every clone pays for it forever. Images that
# a doc actually links to should live somewhere a doc can link to.
screenshots/

# The release token. Ignored BEFORE the file exists, because the failure here is not recoverable the
# way a stray binary is: a token pushed to a public repo is compromised the moment it lands, and
# rewriting history does not un-compromise it. build/secrets.example.ps1 is the one that is tracked.
build/secrets.ps1
.env

# Test / coverage
TestResults/
*.coverage
*.trx

# Parity-run scratch (see README "Checking against the reference implementation")
py.txt
cs.txt
